  "20,000 simulated home batteries of 5\u201311.5 kW and 10\u201320 kWh each (165 MW and 300 MWh in all), in all four cities: Houston (7,000), Dallas\u2013Fort Worth (8,000), San Antonio (2,600) and Austin (2,400).",
  "Batteries never go below 20% charge (a safety reserve), and a round trip (charge, then discharge) returns 90% of the energy.",
  "One cycle means using a battery's full usable energy once, from 100% down to the 20% reserve.",
